Build passes. Here is what changed in `sw.js`:

- **Navigation / `index.html`**: network-first. The browser tries the network, caches the fresh response, and falls back to the cached copy only when offline. Deployed users now get new HTML immediately.
- **`assets/` files**: cache-first unchanged. Vite's content hashes make this safe.
- **Everything else** (manifest, etc.): stale-while-revalidate. Cached copy is served instantly; the cache is refreshed in the background.
- **`CACHE_NAME`** bumped to `"dpd-v2"`, which triggers the activate handler to delete the old `dpd-v1` cache on first run.
